# Single source of truth for the terminal/editor color palettes.
# Sourced directly by bash (dot_config/theme/theme.sh) and parsed by Neovim.
# Colors are ordered by luminance within each mode: BG lightest for light
# mode / darkest for dark mode, FG the opposite, ACCENT1-3 in between.

LIGHT_BG=#fefae0
LIGHT_FG=#283618
LIGHT_ACCENT1=#606c38
LIGHT_ACCENT2=#dda15e
LIGHT_ACCENT3=#bc6c25

DARK_BG=#0d1b2a
DARK_FG=#e0e1dd
DARK_ACCENT1=#1b263b
DARK_ACCENT2=#415a77
DARK_ACCENT3=#778da9

# 16-slot ANSI palette (OSC 4), "semantic" fill: conventional hues kept
# recognizable (red/green/yellow/etc. still read as such for git, ls,
# diagnostics) but saturation/lightness tuned to each mode's mood. Slots
# that map naturally onto the five base colors above reuse them exactly;
# the rest (mostly red/magenta and the bright variants) are hand-tuned to
# match. Index order is the standard ANSI 0-15: black, red, green, yellow,
# blue, magenta, cyan, white, then the bright counterparts of each.

LIGHT_COLOR0=#283618
LIGHT_COLOR1=#a8422f
LIGHT_COLOR2=#606c38
